WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:06.095
"Rocket Girl!" Wukong said, pulling out his iron bar.

2
00:00:06.096 --> 00:00:09.013
The crowd broke apart as people ran away.

3
00:00:09.014 --> 00:00:13.089
Wukong leaped, and Roxy got ready to fight.

4
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:19.493
"Ouch!" Wukong suddenly fell and rolled around, holding his head tightly and crying.

5
00:00:19.494 --> 00:00:22.960
Roxy noticed the Tang Monk speaking softly.

6
00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:26.029
"What's going on?" she thought.

7
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:33.024
"Master, please stop—I'm sorry!" Wukong cried.

8
00:00:33.025 --> 00:00:39.951
The Tang Monk stopped speaking, and Wukong took a deep breath and stood up.

9
00:00:39.952 --> 00:00:43.083
Slowly he approached the Tang Monk.

10
00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:45.369
The Tang Monk folded his arms.

11
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:48.209
"You should be ashamed of yourself."

12
00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:53.172
Wukong stared at the ground.

13
00:00:53.173 --> 00:01:01.247
Bajie giggled. "Do the Tight Headband spell again, Master—Wukong deserves it!"

14
00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:03.858
The Tang Monk glared at Bajie.

15
00:01:03.859 --> 00:01:06.366
"You should be ashamed too, Bajie.

16
00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:11.903
You can't just take over a city like this. It's wrong."

17
00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:18.057
"You two are truly awful sometimes," Wujing said.

18
00:01:18.058 --> 00:01:21.055
"I agree!" Roxy said.

19
00:01:21.056 --> 00:01:26.745
"I'm sorry, Master, but sometimes it's hard to be good," Wukong said.

20
00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:31.519
"You must learn to control yourself," the Tang Monk said.

21
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.899
Mayor Bloom approached the monk and Wukong, looking nervous.

22
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.216
"Are you in charge here?" the Tang Monk asked.

23
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:40.650
The mayor nodded.

24
00:01:40.651 --> 00:01:42.736
The Tang Monk bowed.

25
00:01:42.737 --> 00:01:48.837
"I apologize for the trouble my companions caused, and I hope you will forgive them."

26
00:01:48.838 --> 00:01:52.731
"Sorry," Wukong and Bajie mumbled.

27
00:01:52.732 --> 00:01:58.469
Mayor Bloom cleared his throat. "I accept your apology."

28
00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.991
Wukong turned to the Tang Monk. "I'll be right back, Master."

29
00:02:03.992 --> 00:02:07.284
Wukong hurried to police headquarters.

30
00:02:07.285 --> 00:02:10.285
All the police officers were behind bars.

31
00:02:10.286 --> 00:02:13.519
"Release the prisoners!" he demanded.

32
00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:21.428
A chimpanzee guard unlocked the jail cells, and the officers stepped out.

33
00:02:21.429 --> 00:02:26.983
Detective Smith gave Wukong a suspicious look. "What's going on, Wukong?"

34
00:02:26.984 --> 00:02:32.731
"I'm not king anymore, so Mayor Bloom can go back to ruling this kingdom," Wukong said.

35
00:02:32.732 --> 00:02:38.881
Detective Smith frowned. "It's not a kingdom."

36
00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:43.716
Back at City Hall, Wukong opened the portal.

37
00:02:43.717 --> 00:02:53.307
"Return to the Fruit and Flower Mountain!" he told his army.

38
00:02:53.308 --> 00:02:57.497
Roxy was talking to the Tang Monk, Bajie, and Wujing.

39
00:02:57.498 --> 00:03:00.367
Terrell, Mara, and Jack hurried over.

40
00:03:00.368 --> 00:03:04.684
"Rocket Girl!" Terrell said. "It's great to see you!"

41
00:03:04.685 --> 00:03:09.537
"You saved Metro City again!" Mara said.

42
00:03:09.538 --> 00:03:15.628
Roxy laughed. "Actually, the Tang Monk saved the city."

43
00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:22.873
"It's nice to meet you all," the Tang Monk said.

44
00:03:22.874 --> 00:03:31.491
He called to Wukong. "We must continue our journey now!"

45
00:03:31.492 --> 00:03:35.019
Rumble! Someone's stomach growled.

46
00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:42.011
The Tang Monk groaned. "Bajie! Do you ever stop thinking about food?"

47
00:03:42.012 --> 00:03:47.418
Bajie snorted. "It wasn't me!"

48
00:03:47.419 --> 00:03:51.718
"Of course it was you," Wukong said.

49
00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:56.808
Wujing nodded. "You're always hungry, Bajie."

50
00:03:56.809 --> 00:04:01.196
Bajie held up his hands. "But—but—"

51
00:04:01.197 --> 00:04:06.259
"It was actually me," Mara said. "I'm hungry."

52
00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.075
Bajie snorted again.

53
00:04:09.076 --> 00:04:13.342
"I told you it wasn't me! I am hungry though."

54
00:04:13.343 --> 00:04:15.864
Everyone laughed.

55
00:04:15.865 --> 00:04:18.907
"Let's have a picnic in the park," Jack said.

56
00:04:18.908 --> 00:04:21.716
"Afterward you can continue your journey."

57
00:04:21.717 --> 00:04:27.243
The Tang Monk smiled. "That sounds nice."

58
00:04:27.244 --> 00:04:33.617
After buying sandwiches at a deli, everyone headed into Metro City Park.

59
00:04:33.618 --> 00:04:38.007
As they sat down, dark clouds rolled overhead.

60
00:04:38.008 --> 00:04:42.203
Boom! Boom! Lightning lit up the sky.

61
00:04:42.204 --> 00:04:44.701
Raindrops began to fall.

62
00:04:44.702 --> 00:04:46.742
Terrell's shoulders slumped.

63
00:04:46.743 --> 00:04:50.714
"Now we can't have a picnic. A storm is coming!"

64
00:04:50.715 --> 00:04:56.294
"That's not a storm." Wukong pulled out his iron bar.

65
00:04:56.295 --> 00:05:01.930
"It's an army of demons!"

